info-paper-scp-035-content =
    Object Number: SCP-035
    
    Object Class: Keter
    
    Special Containment Procedures: SCP-035 is to be contained within a sealed glass box with walls at least 10 centimeters thick. The box, in turn, must be kept in a chamber with steel, iron, or lead walls. The chamber door must remain locked with at least three locks at all times; entry is permitted only when personnel access is required. Access must be guarded by at least two (2) armed security personnel at all times. Security personnel must remain outside the chamber and under no circumstances enter the interior. A qualified psychologist must also be present nearby at all times. Personnel involved in research must under no circumstances come into contact with SCP-035. Every two (2) weeks, SCP-035 must be moved to a new box, with the remnants of the previous one disposed of via SCP-101, as the latter does not exhibit susceptibility to the degrading effects of SCP-035. Any individual who comes into contact with SCP-035 while the entity is possessed must receive immediate psychological assistance.
    
    Description: SCP-035 appears as a white porcelain comedian's mask, although the mask periodically takes the form of a tragic figure. When this occurs, all existing images of SCP-035, including photographs, video recordings, and even hand-drawn paintings, spontaneously change to reproduce the new appearance of the object.
    
    A viscous, unappealing, and highly corrosive liquid continuously oozes from the oral and ocular orifices of SCP-035. The chemical composition of this liquid remains unknown. Any object that comes into contact with the liquid slowly decomposes into its elemental components, with the period of complete decomposition varying depending on the material from which the object is composed. Since glass demonstrated the greatest resistance to the degrading effects of SCP-035, it was selected as the material for the containment container. Living organisms that come into contact with the liquid undergo a nearly identical effect, with no possibility of recovery. The emission of liquid is observed only from the front side of the object, but does not occur or is not visible from the back side.
    
    Subjects located at a distance of 1.5 to 2 meters from SCP-035, or those establishing visual contact with it, experience an extremely strong desire to put the object on themselves. When SCP-035 is placed on a subject's face, the subject's brain impulse system is overridden and suppressed by an alternative impulse originating from SCP-035, resulting in the death of the subject's brain, thereby causing the subject to become the embodiment of the personality contained within SCP-035. The bodies of "possessed" subjects decompose at an accelerated rate, soon reaching a state barely distinguishable from a mummified corpse. Nevertheless, SCP-035 demonstrates the ability to maintain cognitive control over significantly damaged bodies, even at levels of decomposition where mechanical movement is no longer possible. The effect does not manifest when placed on an animal's snout.
    
    Communication with SCP-035 proved informative. Researchers uncovered details regarding several SCP objects as well as general history, as SCP-035 apparently witnessed numerous significant historical events. SCP-035 exhibits a high level of intelligence and charm, addressing any interlocutor with great courtesy and flattery. The object successfully passed all proposed tests for intelligence and wit, during which it was determined that SCP-035 possesses photographic memory.
    
    However, psychological analysis revealed an extraordinary propensity for manipulation on the part of SCP-035, coupled with the ability to sharply and radically influence the mental state of an interlocutor. SCP-035 displays sadistic tendencies; for example, one interlocutor was convinced to commit suicide during a simple conversation, while several others were converted into nearly mindless servants. SCP-035 claims to have a deep understanding of the mechanisms of human thought and, given sufficient time, can radically alter the beliefs of any interlocutor.
