info-paper-scp-049-content =
    Object Number: SCP-049
    
    Object Class: Euclid
    
    Special Containment Procedures: SCP-049 is to be held in a standard humanoid reinforced containment cell in Sector 02, Site-19. Prior to any transport attempts, SCP-049 is to be sedated. During transport, SCP-049 must be secured in a Class 3 humanoid restraint system (with a collar and stretch limiters) under the constant supervision of at least two armed guards.
    
    As a general rule, SCP-049 interacts with most Foundation personnel. However, any sudden changes in behavior are to be stopped by force. During such outbursts, personnel are to avoid direct contact with the subject at all costs. It has been established that the application of lavender multifida (L. multifida) may have a calming effect on the subject in the event of aggression. Once sedated, SCP-049 generally becomes more cooperative and is returned to the containment cell, offering virtually no resistance.
    
    To facilitate continued containment of SCP-049, a recently deceased animal carcass (typically a cow or other large mammal) is to be provided to the entity once every two weeks for examination. Carcasses that become SCP-049-2 are to be removed from SCP-049's containment cell and destroyed by incineration. It has been decided to prohibit further human experimentation on SCP-049; therefore, all requests regarding human test subjects are to be denied.
    
    Temporary Addendum to Containment Procedures: (See Addendum 049.3) Per Order No. 049.S19.17.1 of the Containment Committee, SCP-049 is prohibited from direct interaction with Foundation personnel. Additionally, no carcasses are to be provided to the subject for anatomical experiments. This measure is to remain in effect indefinitely and may only be revoked once a consensus is reached regarding the long-term containment of SCP-049.
    
    Description: SCP-049 is a humanoid entity approximately 190 cm tall, resembling a medieval plague doctor. At first glance, it appears that SCP-049 is wearing a thick robe and a ceramic mask characteristic of this profession; however, based on these items of clothing, they have gradually grown from the body of SCP-049 itself and are currently indistinguishable from what they might conceal. Nevertheless, X-rays reveal that beneath this outer layer, SCP-049 possesses a skeleton similar to that of a human.
    
    SCP-049 is capable of speaking many languages, though it primarily prefers English and Old French. SCP-049's personality is generally friendly; the subject readily interacts with Foundation personnel. However, if, in the subject's opinion, something nearby is identified as "The Plague," it becomes extremely irritable and, at times, outright aggressive. The nature of this "Plague" remains unclear to Foundation researchers, but it appears to hold particular significance for SCP-049.
    
    SCP-049 displays open aggression toward those it deems infected by "The Plague," in which cases it is often necessary to restrain it. With freedom of movement, SCP-049 typically attempts to kill such a subject; SCP-049 is capable of halting all biological functions in an organism through direct contact with exposed body parts. The mechanism of this phenomenon is unknown; autopsy results of victims killed by SCP-049 in this manner are inconclusive in all cases. SCP-049 expresses regret or remorse regarding these deaths, stating that the victims did not try to fight "The Plague," although it usually attempts to perform a primitive operation on the corpse using instruments it constantly carries in a black medical bag. The operation does not always result in a "success," but often leads to the creation of SCP-049-2.
    
    SCP-049-2 are reanimated corpses of subjects operated on by SCP-049. Based on external signs, they do not retain memories or intellectual skills and are endowed only with basic motor skills and response mechanisms. Overall, they are largely immobile, moving rarely and aimlessly, but when prompted or commanded by SCP-049, they can become extremely aggressive. SCP-049-2 possess active biological functions, though they radically differ from known modern human physiology. Despite these differences, SCP-049 frequently asserts that the subjects have been "cured."
