info-paper-scp-096-content =
    Object Number: SCP-096
    
    Object Class: Euclid
    
    Special Containment Procedures: SCP-096 must be kept in its containment cell at all times (a sealed steel cube measuring 5x5x5 meters). Weekly inspections for any cracks or openings are mandatory. No video surveillance or optical devices are permitted inside SCP-096's cell. Security personnel must use pre-installed pressure sensors and laser detectors to ensure SCP-096 remains within the cell.
    
    All photographs, videos, or descriptions of SCP-096's appearance are strictly prohibited without the approval of Doctor ███ and O5-█.
    
    Description: SCP-096 is a humanoid entity approximately 2.38 meters tall. The subject exhibits a low muscle mass; preliminary body mass analysis indicates mild malnutrition. The arms are disproportionately large relative to the subject's body, with each measuring approximately 1.5 meters in length. The skin is largely depigmented, and signs of hair on the body are absent.
    
    SCP-096's jaws can open four times wider than the norm for an average human. Other facial features are similar to those of an average human, except for the eyes, which are also depigmented. It is currently unknown whether SCP-096 is blind. There are no indications of higher brain functions; its sentience remains unconfirmed.
    
    Generally, SCP-096 is extremely calm; pressure sensors in the cell indicate that it spends most of its day pacing along the eastern wall. However, when anyone sees the face of SCP-096, whether directly, on video footage, or even on a photograph, it enters a state of extreme emotional distress. SCP-096 covers its face with its hands and begins screaming, weeping, and muttering incoherently. Approximately one to two (1-2) minutes after the initial sighting, SCP-096 runs toward the individual who saw its face (hereafter referred to as SCP-096-1).
