info-paper-scp-173-content =
    Object Number: SCP-173
    
    Object Class: Euclid
    
    Special Containment Procedures: SCP-173 must be kept in a locked containment unit at all times. When personnel visit the SCP-173 containment unit, at least three individuals must enter the unit, and the door must be immediately locked behind them. Two individuals must maintain direct eye contact with SCP-173 until all personnel have exited the unit and it has been locked.
    
    Description: Arrived in Site-19 in 1993. Origin is currently unknown. Constructed from concrete and rebar with traces of Krylon aerosol paint. SCP-173 is sentient and extremely hostile. The object cannot move while within line of sight. When working with SCP-173, eye contact must never be broken. Personnel designated to enter the containment unit are instructed to warn each other before blinking. The object is reported to attack by breaking the neck at the base of the skull, or by strangulation. In the event of an attack, personnel should employ Class-4 dangerous object containment procedures.
    
    Personnel report the grinding noise emanating from the containment unit when no one is present inside. This is considered normal, and any changes in this behavior must be immediately reported to the current HMCL curator.
    
    The reddish-brown substance on the floor is a mixture of feces and blood. The origin of these substances is unknown. Corpses must be cleaned every two weeks.
