info-paper-scp-457-content =
    Object Number: SCP-457
    
    Object Class: Euclid/Potential Keter
    
    Special Containment Procedures: SCP-457 must be contained in a 5m x 5m room equipped with an explosion-proof observation window and additional protection. All internal surfaces must be coated with a fire-resistant material (asbestos-cement or perlite) with a thickness of 22.9 cm (9 inches). Access to the room must consist of at least two airtight, temperature-controlled compartments that can be sealed in the event of an emergency. The room containing SCP-457 must maintain high humidity; the floor must be equipped with a drainage system, continuously operating fine-mist water sprinklers, and emergency fire hoses capable of generating a water pressure of at least 2.1 MPa. SCP-457 is permitted to stand on a special protrusion on the wall of the room, which is out of reach of the water; however, this provides the object with only minimal protection and opportunities to maintain its form.
    
    All personnel entering the containment area must wear full Class A fire-resistant, temperature-controlled suits. Entry into the SCP-457 containment room is permitted only for groups of three, two of whom must be equipped with high-strength ballistic shields and emergency fire extinguishers. Entry into the containment area is authorized solely for the purpose of providing the object with its daily ration of combustible materials, as well as inspecting and repairing damage to the room or sprinkler system.
    
    In the event that SCP-457 attempts to attack personnel, fire extinguishers and fire hoses must be used until the object retreats into its containment room.
    
    In the event of violations of containment procedures, additional sprinklers must be activated, and personnel must be supplied with ballistic shields and fire extinguishers.
    
    Description: SCP-457 is a sentient entity composed of fire. The exact form of the object is unknown; it has not been seen or detected by any means, but it forms itself from fire that it creates itself. If the object has sufficient fuel, it takes the form of a human. The simplest form is a flame tongue the size of a matchstick. In this form, SCP-457 has limited functionality and is indistinguishable from ordinary fire, except for its ability to "flare up," burning people, and independently "jump" onto combustible materials or sources of fire, absorbing them.
    
    As it grows, SCP-457 can assume more complex forms; additionally, as the size of the object increases and it gains access to a large amount of fuel, its intelligence level increases. The thought process of SCP-457 is unknown, but upon reaching a sufficiently large size, it always takes a humanoid form surrounded by flames. SCP-457 is capable of communication, creating letters with fire and burning them onto walls or other surfaces. Occasionally, it speaks using superheated air and the crackling of flames. Upon reaching a certain size, the object splits into two entities, each of which, in turn, is capable of division. However, SCP-457 instances are aggressive towards one another and always attempt to absorb or extinguish a copy, especially if they have limited access to fuel.
    
    The behavior of SCP-457 is very predictable, as its goals consist solely of finding large reserves of combustible materials and spreading. The danger lies in the increase in the object's intelligence as it grows and its ability to learn and mimic human behavior. This leads to SCP-457 intentionally damaging and disabling sprinklers, and in rare cases, preparing complex traps. There have been instances where the object attempted to deceive or convince personnel to release it or provide it with more combustible materials. Due to the unique structure of SCP-457, its changing intelligence level, and its reluctance to engage, no precise analogy can be drawn between its thought process and human cognition.
    
    SCP-457 was captured in the summer of 2007 in ██████, █████, following numerous forest fires caused by the object. It is unknown where and how SCP-457 originally originated. An investigation is ongoing regarding the object's involvement in other major fires.
# [AUTO_EN]
info-paper-scp-939-content =
    Object Number: SCP-939
    
    Object Class: Keter
    
    Special Containment Procedures: SCP-939-1, -3, -19, -53, -89, -96, -98, -99, and -109 are to be contained in Cell 1163-A or 1163-B. Both cells measure 10x10x3 meters and are located in the Militarized Biocontainment Sector 14. Both cells are equipped with climate control systems; the interior is maintained at reduced pressure. Cell walls are reinforced concrete. Access is via a decontamination chamber, the inner door of which is made of steel and is airtight. Observation windows are constructed from layered bulletproof glass 10 cm thick, with a metal mesh under 100 kilovolts of tension between the layers. Relative humidity inside cells is 100%, and temperature is -16° C. Observation of the entities is conducted via cameras operating in the infrared spectrum. Access to SCP-939, containment cells, and observation rooms requires Level 4 personnel authorization.
    
    SCP-939-101 has been dissected; parts of its body are stored in cryogenic chambers 939-101A through 939-101M in Bio-Research Zone 12. Access to SCP-939-101 requires authorization from two or more Level 3 personnel, one of whom must be present during experiments or research. Simultaneous work with the contents of only one cryogenic chamber 939-101 is permitted. When handling SCP-939-101 tissue samples, their internal temperature must be monitored; if it exceeds 10° C, samples must be returned to the cryogenic chamber and work must be suspended for at least seventy-two (72) hours. No other criteria, aside from temperature, apply to the duration of work with tissue samples—unrestricted time is permitted if the researcher can ignore the object's mumbling and pleas to be released.
    
    Containment cells are to be inspected biweekly. During inspection, SCP-939 is transferred to an adjacent cell. During this time, the cell door and windows must be inspected for damage; if necessary, they should be repaired or replaced.
    
    When working with SCP-939, they must be thoroughly sedated, regardless of the type of work. This includes transferring entities between cells. See Document No. 939-TE4 for experiment and cell transfer protocols.
    
    When working with SCP-939, as well as when visiting areas where SCP-939 previously resided, personnel must wear Class C chemical protection suits. After work, personnel must undergo standard decontamination procedures to prevent the spread of amnestics.
    
    In light of incident ABCA14-939-3, all non-D-class personnel involved in work with SCP-939 must wear two waterproof electronic pulse monitors. Monitors transmit signals to a monitoring system equipped with an independent power supply and at least one backup power source. In the event of zero readings or failure of both monitors, the wearer is to be considered dead; personnel must ignore all verbal statements made by the individual. A breach of containment protocol alarm is also automatically triggered. Security personnel responding to the alarm must also wear monitors.
    
    All SCP-939 entities must have tracking beacons implanted subcutaneously upon capture.
    
    Description: SCP-939 are warm-blooded pack predators, some of whose organs and systems are atrophied like troglodytes. SCP-939 skin is highly permeable to moisture, red, and semi-transparent due to saturation with a substance resembling hemoglobin. The average height of a standing SCP-939 entity is 2.2 meters, and weight is 250 kg, though significant deviations may occur. Each of the four limbs has three clawed digits, opposite a thumb. Limbs are covered in bristles, which significantly enhance SCP-939's climbing ability. Heads are elongated; there are no eyes or eye sockets, nor is there a cranial vault. SCP-939 jaws are equipped with pointed teeth that dimly glow red. Jaw and tooth structure resembles that of hauliods, with teeth reaching six centimeters in length. Thermoreceptor pits are located on the outer side of the jaws. Along the spine, covered in spines, are light-sensitive patches. Spines reach 16 centimeters in length and appear sensitive to air currents and atmospheric pressure.
    
    Many vital systems are absent in SCP-939: there are no central or peripheral nervous systems, circulatory system, or gastrointestinal tract. The respiratory system of SCP-939 is atrophied and appears to serve only for exhaling AMN-C227 (see below). It appears that SCP-939 do not require food to sustain life and are incapable of digesting ingested matter. Consumed SCP-939 tissues accumulate in the respiratory system and are regurgitated when their accumulation becomes too great for normal system function. Despite the absence of vital systems, SCP-939 are viviparous (See Appendix 10-16-1991).
    
    SCP-939's preferred method for luring prey is mimicking human speech using the voices of previously killed victims, although there have been cases of active nocturnal hunting and mimicking the sounds of other animals. Often, what SCP-939 utter sounds like distress; attempts have been made to determine whether SCP-939 understand what is being said or are merely repeating previously heard words. It is unknown exactly how SCP-939 recognize voices; there are documented cases of mimicking the voice of a victim who never spoke in their presence. Voice analysis of SCP-939 is unable to distinguish between SCP-939 speech and victim speech. For this reason, it is strongly recommended to refrain from voice identification systems in all facilities housing SCP-939 entities. Victims of SCP-939 are typically killed with a single bite to the base of the skull or neck; the jaws of these creatures can develop pressures exceeding 350 atmospheres.
    
    SCP-939 exhale a low concentration of Class C amnestics (hereinafter AMN-C227). AMN-C227 causes temporary anterograde amnesia, suppressing memory formation for the entire duration of its action plus approximately thirty minutes. The substance is colorless, tasteless, and odorless; the EC50 is 0.0015 mg per minute per cubic meter. In well-ventilated rooms or outdoors, EC50 drops significantly but still poses a threat. After 60 minutes of exposure, AMN-C227 dissolves in the blood. The disorientation and mild hallucinations experienced after exiting an AMN-C227-saturated area resemble post-effects from various psychoactive substances, making it easy to confuse one for the other.
